14:50:17 | INFO | 🤖 Target initial answer: Creators of free apps and websites can make money in several common ways: - **Advertising:** Showing banner ads, video ads, sponsored posts, or search ads. They earn per view, click, or purchase. - **Freemium upgrades:** The basic service is free, but users pay for premium features, extra storage, no ads, customization, etc. - **Subscriptions:** Some features or content require a monthly or yearly payment. - **In-app purchases:** Common in games and apps—users buy virtual items, credits, extra features, or content. - **Affiliate commissions:** The app recommends products or services and earns a commission when users buy through its links. - **Selling products or services:** A free website may promote a company’s paid consulting, courses, physical products, software, or other services. - **Sponsorships and partnerships:** Brands pay to be featured or associated with the app/site. - **Donations or crowdfunding:** Users voluntarily support the creator through platforms like Patreon, tips, or one-time donations. - **Licensing or business plans:** Individual users may get a free version, while companies pay for team, enterprise, or API access. - **Data and analytics:** Some services use aggregated, anonymized usage data for research or advertising insights. Responsible companies disclose this and give users privacy controls. Often, only a small percentage of users pay, while free users help grow the audience that makes advertising, referrals, or premium upgrades valuable.
